| **Process‑level security** | Secrets stored in a file live on disk and can be read by anyone with filesystem access. A secrets manager can enforce IAM policies and rotate automatically. |
| **Lack of rotation & audit** | `.env` files are static; rotating keys requires manual edit, redeploy, and may slip through code‑review. Secrets services provide versioned rotation & audit logs. |

