| **A2 – Broken Authentication** | No authentication, open `/users`. | Added **JWT‑based `authenticateJWT`** middleware; all `/api/v1/*` routes are protected. Replace with your auth provider (OAuth2, session cookies, etc.) as needed. |
| **A3 – Sensitive Data Exposure** | `/users` leaks email addresses; no HTTPS. | Authentication prevents unauthorized access. Use **HTTPS** termination (e.g., Nginx, Cloudflare, or `https.createServer`). Also enforce **HSTS** via Helmet. |
| **A4 – XML External Entities (XXE)** | Not applicable (no XML parsing). | N/A – just avoid XML parsers or configure them securely if added later. |
| **A5 – Security Misconfiguration** | Missing security headers, CORS open, no rate‑limit. | **Helmet** adds CSP, HSTS, X‑Content‑Type‑Options, etc.; **CORS** whitelist; **rateLimit**; centralised error handling; environment‑based config. |
